// spec: DCL-006, INI-003
//
// The other side of 0146: a class inheriting from a module named BELOW it.
//
// ⚠️ Refused, and the message is about the NAME rather than about inheritance.
// A module runs at its clause [INI-003], so nothing has bound 'Shape' when
// this declaration is reached -- the same failure as reading any name that is
// not there yet [DCL-016], which is what makes hoisting a class's build
// conditional rather than unconditional.

WriteLn ('root, before the import');

class Circle (Shape);
begin
    constructor Init (); begin end
end

uses 'modules/Shape';

WriteLn (Circle ().Name ());
